  "notes": {
    "mod_writer": "**DslWriter**\n\nEvery model edit becomes a Roslyn `DocumentEditor` rewrite here. Never a string rebuild, never `NormalizeWhitespace()` \u2014 both destroy trivia, and trivia is what makes a diff readable.\n\nIf the round-trip fixtures fail, this file is wrong. Not the test.",
    "mod_engine": "**StemmaEngine**\n\nThe fa\u00e7ade the web layer is allowed to call, and the boundary the purity rule defends. It references Roslyn and `Stemma.Model`. It does not know that HTTP exists.",
    "sys_git": "**Git working tree**\n\nThe store. `Architecture/*.cs` and `Views/*.cs` are the model; `stemma.layout.json` is presentation. Branch, blame, revert and review all work because there is nothing else to keep in sync.",
    "mod_render": "**DiagramRenderer**\n\nDrives a bare canvas through Playwright and screenshots the content bounds. Starts a short-lived host per render, which is why two renders never fight over one workspace.\n\nIt exits `0` whatever it drew \u2014 see `risk_exitzero`.",
    "mod_hub": "**SignalR hub**\n\nThe operation stream in, the delta broadcast out. Modelled as one `twoway` flow rather than two arrows because it is one round trip.",
    "con_fidelity": "The rule that outranks every other argument in this repository.\n\nIt is not a policy document. It is `DslWriter` plus minimal, realistic and deliberately pathological fixtures per operation."
  },
  "customProps": {}
